infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Layout vs template: persist or remount on navigation
  desc A layout keeps the same instance and state across soft navigation; a template throws it away and remounts every time
  compares
    - label layout.tsx — persists
      children
        - label Same component instance stays mounted
          desc React keeps it across shared-layout soft navigation
        - label Client state survives the navigation
          desc Collapsed sidebar, scroll position, a playing video
        - label Server code does not re-run
          desc So layout data goes stale after a mutation
        - label Refresh it deliberately, never via effect
          desc revalidatePath in the action, or router.refresh
    - label template.tsx — remounts
      children
        - label New instance on every navigation
          desc The remounting twin of layout, by design
        - label Client state resets each navigation
          desc The subtree starts fresh every time
        - label Re-renders and re-fetches each time
          desc Server code runs again on every navigation
        - label Reach for it when state must reset
          desc The rarely-needed exception, not the default
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
